You noticed that wolves lost interest in you and preferred not to come close, so you stopped showing your teeth and made yourself comfortable on the grass.
After some time you heard voices in the alley. Flashlight beams were sliding over the roads, enclosures, and grass. Soon three men came up to the enclosure you were in. Two of them definitely were cops. You bared your teeth again.
"Are you sure that everything is normal, old man?" harshly asked one of the cops. "Are your animals all here?" They lit the enclosure with the beams. It lit up the pack and you. 
"Hey, light up this one again!"
The beam returned. You froze, your muscles strained.
"This one doesn't look like mine... What does it have on its neck? Is that a cell phone?"
You decided not to find out what was on your neck, but instead made another jump over the fence and rushed off down the road. The policemen obviously weren't as fast as you were and were slow to react, but then they grabbed their guns and opened fire at you. You shuddered and shrieked when one of the bullets hit you. Trying ignore the pain, you hurried to run as far as possible. Luckily you met no more cops on your way.